# Until the P5 cutover site/ holds two trees: the HTML pages and their assets,
# which are the knowledge base's source and are never reformatted here, and the
# Astro workspace beside them. So everything at the top is ignored and the
# workspace's own files are named back in.
/*
!/src/
!/astro.config.mjs
!/eslint.config.js
!/vitest.config.ts
!/tsconfig.json
!/package.json
!/.prettierrc.json

# The generated build input, by the same ownership rule the root .gitignore
# states: every .md under src/content/docs/ is a page the mirror copied from
# docs/, every index.mdx below the top folder a hub gen-site-hubs.ts wrote,
# every page of map/ one gen-map-pages.ts wrote.
# Formatting a generator's output means the check passes only until the next
# `npm run gen`. The hand-written pages (the top index.mdx) are formatted.
/src/content/docs/**/*.md
/src/content/docs/*/**/index.mdx
/src/content/docs/map/*.mdx

# The built site. tools/src/site/site-format.ts shapes it as the build's last
# step; prettier's one width setting would pull that shape's two rules in
# opposite directions (spec formatter-C8). Named although /* covers it, so it
# stays when the top-level pages leave at the cutover.
/dist/
